  "description": "With a revised geometry, this year’s Provincial Trail line prefers trails to bike lanes, just like you. The geometry isn’t the only update you’ll notice — the second generation Provincial Trail 1 also gets a few upgrades to make your time on two wheels easier and more comfortable. Shimano’s Cues drivetrain puts 20 hill flattening gears at your fingertips and delivers solid performance and easy maintenance. Reliable mechanical disc brakes keep you in control of your speed and are a big step-up from rim brakes. The revised frame now wears a carbon fibre fork, replacing the first generation’s chromoly fork. This change reduces weight and complements the plush 45mm tires, helping smooth out those rough gravel grinds. And when you can’t enjoy the road less travelled, the Trail 1 is also a great performer on your weekday commute.\n\nLight and strong 6000-series aluminum frame has a stable trail-ready geometry.\n\nInternal cable routing uses alloy cable-stops that allow you to customize your setup and add a dropper post should you wish to do so\n\nCarbon fibre fork reduces weight and offers a smoother ride.\n\nFrame is equipped with eyelets for fenders, racks, bottle cages and bag mounts\n\n12x100mm thru-axle fork and 12x142mm frame makes it easy to switch between these adventure-ready wheels and road-specific ones\n\nFrame and fork clearance allows for tires that measures up to 50mm in width\n\n2 x 10-speed Shimano Cues drivetrain provides smooth, reliable shifting, giving a great range for trails or hills.\n\nShimano’s Cues drivetrain provides reliable performance, durability, and easy maintenance – with cross compatibility across the line\n\nCues 46-32T crankset and 11-39T cassette offer a range of gears for all terrain.\n\nCues mechanical disc brakes have plenty of stopping power and aren’t affected by the weather like rim brakes can be.\n\nGravel-friendly bars feature a 16° flare for improved stability when riding in the drops\n\nWTB ST i23 rims are tubeless ready and designed for the rigours of gravel grinds\n\nWTB Vulpine tires are tubeless ready are a fast rolling hybrid of a race-focused cyclocross tire and a grippy gravel tire. Tightly spaced centre lugs reduce rolling resistance and encourage straight line speed, while tightly packed shoulder lugs grab in the corners and on loose terrain.\n\nMEC Gravel seat is comfortable and supportive without getting the way of power delivery.\n\nPart of MEC’s Provincial collection – a versatile series of bags and bikes that are just as useful on your commute, as they are on your gravel grinds and bikepacking adventures\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes are designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics are developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
